# W3.9 (WP65) on Shard, 2 clients on payloads.msav (PayloadsMap.java: a core, a mega, a dagger above it and a
# container of 50 copper below). alpha takes the mega over (unitControl, sent as ctrl+click does) and, with vanilla's
# keys ([ picks up, ] drops), lifts the dagger and sets it down; then lifts the container (requestBuildPayload, as [
# sends it); a deny rule refuses its drop with the rule's message, and once the rule is gone it goes down two tiles
# east (requestDropPayload, as ] sends it, at a set place). The server's tiles and both clients' view of the mega
# follow each change.
#
# Vanilla quirk: a client may never place a dropped building, though its copy of the carrier held it. Likely the
# entity snapshot that empties the carrier's payloads reaches it before the payloadDropped Call, which then has
# nothing to drop. Its tile stays empty until it reloads, and block snapshots of the building skip it ("Missing
# entity"). A vanilla server does it too (bravo, against vanilla-server.sh), so the clients' tiles aren't checked
# after a drop.
allow client-log /Missing entity at stone:air:air\[18,12\]/
#
#   rig/run.sh --vm "$(cat .vm-id)" --server 'mkdir -p maps && cp ~/shard/rig/scenarios/payloads.msav maps/ \
#     && PUSH=~/shard/server/build/install/shard exec "$RIG"/vm/shard-server.sh "payloads sandbox"' \
#     --clients 2 --script rig/scenarios/shard-payloads.rig
timeout 8m

wait port 120s
alpha: join
bravo: join
all: shot joined

# the mega, from alpha's core unit
alpha: expect js "(function(){Call.unitControl(Vars.player, Groups.unit.find(function(u){return u.type == UnitTypes.mega}));return 'sent'})()" /^sent$/ 10s
alpha: expect js "Vars.player.unit().type.name" /^mega$/ 10s
bravo: expect js "Groups.unit.find(function(u){return u.type == UnitTypes.mega}).isPlayer()" /^true$/ 10s

# [ takes the closest dagger first: requestUnitPayload, then pickedUnitPayload to everyone
alpha: press OPEN_BRACKET
alpha: expect js "Vars.player.unit().payloads.size" /^1(\.0)?$/ 10s
bravo: expect js "Groups.unit.count(function(u){return u.type == UnitTypes.dagger})" /^0(\.0)?$/ 10s
all: shot dagger-lifted
# ] sets it down where the mega is: requestDropPayload, then payloadDropped; it comes back as a new unit
alpha: press CLOSE_BRACKET
alpha: expect js "Vars.player.unit().payloads.size" /^0(\.0)?$/ 10s
bravo: expect js "Groups.unit.count(function(u){return u.type == UnitTypes.dagger})" /^1(\.0)?$/ 10s

# the container, three and a half tiles below, within reach: requestBuildPayload, then pickedBuildPayload
alpha: expect js "(function(){Call.requestBuildPayload(Vars.player, Vars.world.build(14, 8));return 'sent'})()" /^sent$/ 10s
alpha: expect js "Vars.player.unit().payloads.size" /^1(\.0)?$/ 10s
bravo: expect js "Vars.world.build(14, 8) == null" /^true$/ 10s
console tile payloads 14 8
wait log server /^tile 14,8 .* block=air / 10s
# bravo's mega holds it too: its team and copper, through the Call and the entity snapshots
bravo: expect js "(function(){var m = Groups.unit.find(function(u){return u.type == UnitTypes.mega});return m.payloads.size + ' ' + (m.payloads.size > 0 ? m.payloads.peek().build.team.id + ' ' + m.payloads.peek().build.items.get(Items.copper) : '-')})()" /^1 1 50$/ 10s
all: shot container-lifted
# a deny rule on dropPayload: the drop is refused with the rule's message, and the mega keeps the container. Drops
# go to (145, 98), tile (18, 12) for a 2x2 block: within the mega's 4-tile margin and clear of the dagger under it, as
# ] sends requestDropPayload with the player's position (] itself checks the ground under the mega first)
console actions payloads deny no-drop dropPayload [scarlet]No dropping here.
wait log server /rule no-drop denies dropPayload/ 10s
alpha: expect js "(function(){Call.requestDropPayload(Vars.player, 145, 98);return 'sent'})()" /^sent$/ 10s
alpha: expect chat /No dropping here/ 10s
alpha: expect js "Vars.player.unit().payloads.size" /^1(\.0)?$/ 10s
console tile payloads 18 12
wait log server /^tile 18,12 .* block=air / 10s
all: shot denied
# without the rule it goes down there
console actions payloads allow no-drop
wait log server /rule no-drop removed/ 10s
alpha: expect js "(function(){Call.requestDropPayload(Vars.player, 145, 98);return 'sent'})()" /^sent$/ 10s
alpha: expect js "Vars.player.unit().payloads.size" /^0(\.0)?$/ 10s
bravo: expect js "Groups.unit.find(function(u){return u.type == UnitTypes.mega}).payloads.size" /^0(\.0)?$/ 10s
console tile payloads 18 12
wait log server /^tile 18,12 .* block=container / 10s
all: shot dropped

assert clean all
assert clean server
